    "evidence_text": "CNTF reverses obesity-induced insulin resistance by activating skeletal muscle AMPK\n\nPulmonary hypertension (PH) causes loss of body weight and inspiratory (diaphragm) muscle dysfunction.\n\nActivation of fast skeletal muscle troponin as a potential therapeutic approach for treating neuromuscular diseases\n\nHowever, less is known about its efficacy in later disease stages and in non-Val30Met mutations.\n\nWe performed a multi-center observational study on symptomatic ATTR patients prescribed to receive Tafamidis.\n\nSixty-one (42 males) patients were recruited.\n\nTafamidis proved safe and well-tolerated.\n\nNeurological function worsened particularly in the first 6 months but progression slowed significantly thereafter.\n\nA higher mBMI at baseline was associated with better preservation of neurological function.\n\nIn conclusion, neuropathy and cardiomyopathy progressed in a significant proportion of patients despite treatment.\n\nBody weight preservation is an important favorable prognostic factor.\n\nOur previous study has shown that autophagy is altered in the mouse model of ALS.\n\nCyclic nucleotide phosphodiesterase isozymes expressed in mouse skeletal muscle.\n\nExercise blood flow patterns within and among rat muscles after training.",
